"""Record the inspected APK and update continuity while retaining earlier approvals/history."""
from pathlib import Path
import difflib,json,shutil
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[5];BASE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent;QA=BASE/'QA'
read=lambda n:json.loads((QA/n).read_text())
build=read('BuildValidation.json');assert build['result']=='Passed';a=read('Artifact.json');old=read('PreviousArtifact.json');seconds=read('Build/summary.json')['durationSeconds'];checks=read('PreflightBoundaryChecks.json')['passed'];h=a['sha256'];size=f"{a['bytes']:,}";delta=a['bytes']-old['bytes']
assert read('OfflinePreflight.json')['status']=='offline_prepared_device_deferred'
report=f'''# Settings recovery Android refresh R2 — complete

[Build reconciliation](QA/BuildValidation.json) · [Compiled owners/callbacks](QA/AfterNative.json) · [Source results](../R1/TestResults.md) · [Final validation](QA/FinalValidation.json) · [Handoff/tool patch](Sources/HandoffChanges.patch).

Current development APK: `Builds/Verification/v1_17_step01/LegendsOfRus-v1.17-step01-development.apk`, **{size} bytes**, SHA256 `{h}`. It now packages acknowledged atomic preference commitment, rejected-save error presentation inside the existing Settings page and callback ownership/reentry protection. Music, SFX, vibration and notification state remain committed preferences when saving is rejected. The same standalone or paused Settings root is retained; existing Russian/English error wording, Close/Back behavior, layout and art are unchanged. All earlier round lifecycle/selection/tutorial/narrative/energy/reward/spending/durable refund recovery remains included. These are local development-build results, not physical or production-store acceptance.

The previous round lifecycle APK, **{old['bytes']:,} bytes**, SHA256 `{old['sha256']}`, is preserved with its inherited checksum under `Builds/Verification/v1_17_step01/BeforeSettingsRefreshR2/`.

Unity **6000.5.9f1**: **160 fresh distinct Edit Mode build-policy/content/preset checks passed**, zero failures/skips. The installed guarded development build succeeded, launcher exit 0 and BuildReport Succeeded, {seconds:.2f}s. Prior same-source R1 **396 distinct passes (311 Play/85 Edit)** remain the runtime/service evidence; no new Play Mode or device run in this build task. **{checks} synthetic/mocked offline preflight checks passed**. Actual default preflight verifies the current artifact and inclusion evidence with zero ADB/device/player-data calls.

Before rebuilding, 67 generated/native owner methods matched the previous APK; afterward **68 owners and six callback regions** match the actual stripped IL2CPP library and Gradle input. The seven Settings owners include the new TryTogglePreference API. Generated preference code validates the index and persistence lock before cloning, flips only its candidate boolean and calls the existing atomic balance commit without Persist. Native TogglePreference checks CanAct, holds/resets its busy guard around the acknowledging call, refreshes committed state and uses the existing InfoPanel on rejection. Unbind rotates ownership before listener removal; Listen captures the current owner. Its actual callback rejects retired binding identity before checking input/button/InfoPanel and invoking the action. Existing localization literals and the error branch are packaged. Prior round transaction, map, tutorial, narrative, energy, rewards and refund flags remain verified. Native method-byte correlation establishes compiled inclusion, separately from physical execution. R1 supplies the actual healthy/rejected/pause/reentry/runtime behavior evidence.

The first Settings callback audit expected a direct IsInteractable call name; IL2CPP emitted the boolean virtual dispatch on the captured Button. The next guard assertion assumed the C# lexical order of the finally assignment; IL2CPP declares its scoped Finally lambda before the try block. The audit now verifies both the boolean dispatch before InfoPanel/action and the generated scoped cleanup before the later refresh, preserving native-byte correlation and rejection ordering. [Audit correction](QA/NativeInitialAuditCorrection.json) records the initial failure. No production change or additional Unity build was required.

Signature, original development certificate, package/version 0.0.0/code 1/ARM64/min 26/target 36/portrait/debug and permissions are retained. ZIP CRC, exact accounting, zero unindexed gaps, 16 KiB alignment and all six ELF load alignments pass. Nine credential DEX/JNI classes and four Java/meta pins remain intact. All **403 ZIP paths** remain: **399 payloads identical and four reviewed changes** (IL2CPP code/metadata and two build identifiers), APK byte delta {delta:+,}. The engine library/bindings and complete player asset pack are byte-identical. All **29,387 packed path/GUID/type rows and eight page object sizes**, including Settings, are unchanged. Settings Revision 5 and required bindings are checked by the temporary build audit; Profile 13/Dialogue 2/Gameplay 24/Victory 12/Daily 5/receipt 2, four stock layouts, 58 story scenes/57 milestones and six pure disposable selectors remain intact.

All **7,839 project inputs remain unchanged** after temporary Editor helper removal and generated Addressables cleanup. The tracked compiler fingerprint was backed up/restored outside the repository. Three generated packing caches are preserved reversibly: first two under `/tmp/lor-settings-android-refresh-r2/BeforeFreshPacking/`, third under `/dev/shm/lor-settings-android-refresh-r2/BeforeFreshPacking/2`. [Mapping](QA/FreshPackingCachePreservation.json) · [Quota recovery](QA/PackingQuotaRecovery.json). Initial third-cache copying hit a /tmp quota; the original directory remained intact. A complete alternative copy was byte-verified before removing that original generated cache and the partial /tmp copy. The unchanged 8 GiB disk guard was satisfied before building; no guard/source/backend/package changes. Two incremental packaging states are preserved under Library/LegendsOfRusPackagingBackups/BeforeSettingsRefreshR2. Approved Splash/art/GUIDs/metas/prefabs/builders/fonts/revisions/settings and pending user edits remain intact.

Eight existing handoff/tool files updated: CurrentTask, ConversationHandoff, SessionLog, DevelopmentSchedule, AndroidGameplayJourney/R1/DeviceChecklist, AndroidGameplayProfile/R1/Usage and canonical Preflight/CheckPreflight. All were backed up; earlier acceptance decisions and dated pins remain historical. New audit sources, C++ snippets, test/inspection records and logs reside in this task folder. APK/sidecar and generated caches remain ignored local artifacts. No Git commit/push, personal journal/credential access, phone/hosting action or store upload occurred.

Human rounds 201–210 remain unrecorded from the user's prior confirmation; no rescan or tuning. All 18 physical rows remain pending. Fresh GameState recovery in R1 is same-process evidence, without Android/process restart acceptance. Physical audibility/haptics/notification delivery, real paid/video settlement, RuStore production readiness and measured profitability remain unverified. Stock-max remains restricted and effects remain last. General Persist/reset/load lifecycle callers and the separate language preference remain outside the Settings patch.

**Next core work:** audit remaining general Persist/reset/load save-recovery paths and scope changes from reproduced defects. Human 201–210 recordings, ratings and story/difficulty observations remain the Chapter 1 acceptance dependency before tuning; phone/hosting remain deferred.
'''
